  bigIdea:
    'Preaching to his own congregation, Pastor Darby warns that many women are getting saved but keeping the world’s motto, sisters over everything: a bond of shared pain with girlfriends and with a women’s ministry that grows stronger than the bond of the gospel and the covenant of marriage. He does not oppose women preaching, but he says a women’s ministry that never teaches what Titus 2 commands, to love husbands, love children and be discreet, ends up pulling wives out of their homes. His cure is order and stability: Yahweh first, then your spouse, then your children; cleave to your mate; stay planted; and let godly friendship replace the old sisterhood.',
