    'The quoted lines are his own words from the archive.org recording, each with its time; his longer arguments are summarized in prose. Verified in the record: the October 2015 Spring Valley High School incident; that enslaved people could not legally marry and that sales broke up families; Alabama’s substitute-father welfare rule and its end in 1968. Stated plainly where the record differs from him: NSSM 200 is a 1974 study of population growth in thirteen developing countries; it is not a document about the Black family or Black men in America. Weighed and corrected by the Word in the lesson: his saying that fathers do not nurture (Ephesians 6:4 gives fathers the charge to bring up children in nurture); his reading that Adam sinned by listening to his wife at all (Genesis 21:12 shows Yahweh telling Abraham to hearken to Sarah; the sin in Eden was hearkening against Yahweh’s Word); his statement that Yahweh hated Ahab for weakness (1 Kings 21 records Ahab’s wickedness and Yahweh’s mercy when he humbled himself). Not repeated here: a figure he gave for the lifespan of homosexual men, a speculation about the adversary’s nature, and an account of a public ritual on plantations; this lesson keeps to what the record of slavery documents.',
