    'In a spiritual-warfare sermon Pastor Darby teaches that the church is in a real war with the kingdom of darkness, and that one of its oldest weapons is seduction: drawing believers into sexual sin and getting them used to sin a little at a time, which he calls absurdity in small doses, until what was once shocking feels normal. Using the West African tradition of a water spirit called the Queen of the Coast and a deliverance account he read aloud, he warns that prayerless Christians are easy targets and praying, fasting Christians are the ones darkness fears. His call: pray, fast, keep the Word in your heart, stop entertaining what you want to be free of, guard your eyes and your marriage, and bless those who provoke you.',
